PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L04U3.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":4,"cefr":"A2b","unit":3,"theme":"Rules and Manners","essential_question":"Why do we need rules and good manners?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS1","title":"You Must Wear Your Uniform: must, mustn't, have to, don't have to","objectives":["Students will be able to use must and have to for rules and obligations.","Students will be able to tell the difference between mustn't (it's not allowed) and don't have to (it's not necessary).","I can explain school rules with must and have to.","I can say \"You mustn't run\" and \"You don't have to bring lunch\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام must وhave to للقواعد والالتزامات.","سيتمكن الطلاب من التمييز بين mustn't (غير مسموح) وdon't have to (غير ضروري).","أستطيع أن أشرح قواعد المدرسة باستخدام must وhave to.","أستطيع أن أقول You mustn't run وYou don't have to bring lunch."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"rule","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rul/","definition":"something that tells you what you must or mustn't do","arabic":"قاعدة / قانون","example":"Our class has five simple rules.","image_id":"GV-L04-U3-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS1-W01"},{"word":"manners","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmænɚz/","definition":"polite ways of behaving with other people","arabic":"آداب / سلوك مهذب","example":"Good manners make everyone feel welcome.","image_id":"GV-L04-U3-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS1-W02"},{"word":"polite","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/pəˈlaɪt/","definition":"showing good manners and respect","arabic":"مهذب","example":"It's polite to say \"please\".","image_id":"GV-L04-U3-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS1-W03"},{"word":"rude","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/rud/","definition":"not polite","arabic":"وقح / غير مهذب","example":"It's rude to interrupt someone.","image_id":"GV-L04-U3-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Use must and have to + base verb for rules and things that are necessary: You must wear a seat belt. I have to get up early.\nmustn't (must not) = it is not allowed – don't do it! You mustn't run in the hall.\ndon't have to = it is not necessary – you can choose: You don't have to bring lunch (but you can). These two are very different!\nmust / have to + base verb = necessary\nmustn't + base verb = not allowed (prohibited)\ndon't / doesn't have to + base verb = not necessary\nhe / she / it → has to / doesn't have to; must never changes.","examples":["Drivers must stop at a red light.","You mustn't touch the paintings in the museum.","I have to finish my homework before dinner.","My dad has to work on Thursday.","You don't have to wear a jacket today – it's warm.","Students mustn't use phones during the exam.","Do we have to bring our books tomorrow?","Visitors must take off their shoes in the mosque."],"common_errors":["✗ You must to wear a helmet. → ✓ You must wear a helmet. (No to after must.)","✗ She have to go now. → ✓ She has to go now. (he/she/it → has to.)","✗ You mustn't bring lunch. (meaning: it's not necessary) → ✓ You don't have to bring lunch. (mustn't = not allowed; don't have to = not necessary.)","✗ He musts study. → ✓ He must study. (must never takes -s.)"],"arabic":"must وhave to + الفعل الأصلي للتعبير عن الضرورة والقواعد: You must wear a seat belt.\nmustn't تعني «ممنوع»: You mustn't run in the hall.\ndon't have to تعني «ليس ضروريًا» (لك أن تختار): You don't have to bring lunch.\nلا نضع to بعد must، ومع he/she/it نقول has to وdoesn't have to."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “You Must Wear Your Uniform: must, mustn't, have to, don't have to”. Let’s learn must / mustn't / have to / don't have to together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U3-LS1 | You Must Wear Your Uniform: must, mustn't, have to, don't have to","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Welcome to Our School!”: Adam is new at our school, so Mr. Khalid is explaining the rules. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Adam is new at our school, so Mr. Khalid is explaining the rules.","visual":"Image GV-L04-U3-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Use must and have to + base verb for rules and things that are necessary: You must wear a seat belt. I have to get up early. mustn't (must not) = it is not allowed – don't do it! You mustn't run in the hall.","on_screen":"must / have to + base verb = necessary • mustn't + base verb = not allowed (prohibited) • don't / doesn't have to + base verb = not necessary","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Drivers must stop at a red light. You mustn't touch the paintings in the museum. I have to finish my homework before dinner.","on_screen":"Drivers must stop at a red light. / You mustn't touch the paintings in the museum. / I have to finish my homework before dinner.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “You must to wear a helmet.” That’s not right. We say: “You must wear a helmet.” No to after must.","on_screen":"✗ You must to wear a helmet.   ✓ You must wear a helmet.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"You mustn't swim here.\" Can you swim here? … Think! … No – it's not allowed. Great job! Now you can say: I can explain school rules with must and have to.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can explain school rules with must and have to.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: must / mustn't / have to / don't have to.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","must وhave to + الفعل الأصلي للتعبير عن الضرورة والقواعد: You must wear a seat belt.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: You must to wear a helmet. — الصحيح: You must wear a helmet.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أشرح قواعد المدرسة باستخدام must وhave to."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Welcome to Our School!","body":"Adam is new at our school, so Mr. Khalid is explaining the rules.\n\"You must wear your uniform every day, and you must arrive before seven o'clock.\nYou mustn't run in the corridors – it's dangerous.\nYou have to bring your own water bottle, but you don't have to bring lunch. The canteen sells healthy food.\"\nAdam asked, \"Do I have to speak English all day?\"\n\"No, you don't have to,\" said Mr. Khalid, \"but you should try! And you should ask for help when you need it.\"\nAdam smiled. \"Thank you. The rules are fair.\"","word_count":96,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"You ___ wear a seat belt in the car. It's the law.","options":["mustn't","must","musts","don't have to"],"answer":"must","explanation":"must / have to + base verb = necessary.","explanation_ar":"الضرورة."},{"q":"You ___ eat in the computer room. It's not allowed.","options":["have to","must","mustn't","don't have to"],"answer":"mustn't","explanation":"mustn't = not allowed.","explanation_ar":"mustn't تعني ممنوع."},{"q":"It's Friday. We ___ go to school.","options":["mustn't","has to","must","don't have to"],"answer":"don't have to","explanation":"don't have to = not necessary.","explanation_ar":"don't have to تعني غير ضروري."},{"q":"My brother ___ wear glasses to read.","options":["must to","has to","have to","haves to"],"answer":"has to","explanation":"he / she / it → has to / doesn't have to.","explanation_ar":"المفرد الغائب ← has to."},{"q":"Players must ___ the referee.","options":["to listen to","listening to","listens to","listen to"],"answer":"listen to","explanation":"No to after must; must has no -s.","explanation_ar":"لا to بعد must."},{"q":"___ I have to sign the paper?","options":["Do","Am","Must","Have"],"answer":"Do","explanation":"he / she / it → has to / doesn't have to.","explanation_ar":"المفرد الغائب ← has to."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write must, mustn't or don't have to. Word bank: must, don't have to, mustn't","items":[{"q":"You ______ cross the road when the light is red.","options":[],"answer":"mustn't","explanation":"mustn't = not allowed.","explanation_ar":"mustn't تعني ممنوع."},{"q":"You ______ buy a ticket. The museum is free.","options":[],"answer":"don't have to","explanation":"don't have to = not necessary.","explanation_ar":"don't have to تعني غير ضروري."},{"q":"Pilots ______ wear their uniform at work.","options":[],"answer":"must","explanation":"must / have to + base verb = necessary.","explanation_ar":"الضرورة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite with has to or doesn't have to.","items":[{"q":"(Hamad / wear a uniform at the club – necessary)  (has to)","options":[],"answer":"Hamad has to wear a uniform at the club.","explanation":"he / she / it → has to / doesn't have to.","explanation_ar":"المفرد الغائب ← has to."},{"q":"(Lina / cook tonight – not necessary)  (doesn't have to)","options":[],"answer":"Lina doesn't have to cook tonight.","explanation":"don't have to = not necessary.","explanation_ar":"don't have to تعني غير ضروري."},{"q":"(my dad / work on Saturday – necessary)  (has to)","options":[],"answer":"My dad has to work on Saturday.","explanation":"he / she / it → has to / doesn't have to.","explanation_ar":"المفرد الغائب ← has to."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write rules you know.","items":[{"q":"At school, we must ___.","options":[],"answer":"At school, we must arrive on time.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must / mustn't / have to / don't have to correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In the library, you mustn't ___.","options":[],"answer":"In the library, you mustn't talk loudly.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must / mustn't / have to / don't have to correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"At home, I have to ___.","options":[],"answer":"At home, I have to make my bed.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must / mustn't / have to / don't have to correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"On Friday, I don't have to ___.","options":[],"answer":"On Friday, I don't have to wake up early.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must / mustn't / have to / don't have to correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In the car, everyone must ___.","options":[],"answer":"In the car, everyone must wear a seat belt.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must / mustn't / have to / don't have to correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Make a sign.","items":[{"q":"Design a sign for the swimming pool with 2 must and 2 mustn't rules.","options":[],"answer":"You must take a shower first. You must swim with an adult. You mustn't run. You mustn't push others.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must / mustn't / have to / don't have to correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 things a new student doesn't have to do at your school.","options":[],"answer":"He doesn't have to bring lunch. He doesn't have to buy new books.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must / mustn't / have to / don't have to correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask your partner \"What do you have to do at home?\" Write 2 answers.","options":[],"answer":"He has to tidy his room. He has to help his little brother.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must / mustn't / have to / don't have to correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Four Corners Grammar","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a sentence frame with a cue word and four possible answers (A–D).","Students walk to the corner with the correct answer.","One student in each corner explains the choice in one sentence.","Correct corner scores a point; continue with the next cue."],"data":[{"label":"You must…"},{"label":"You mustn't…"},{"label":"You have to…"},{"label":"You don't have to…"},{"label":"You should…"},{"label":"You shouldn't…"},{"label":"Do I have to…?"},{"label":"Should I…?"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"We ___ be quiet during the prayer.","options":["don't have to","mustn't","must","musts"],"answer":"must","explanation":"must / have to + base verb = necessary.","explanation_ar":"الضرورة."},{"q":"You ___ play with fire. It's dangerous!","options":["mustn't","don't have to","have","must"],"answer":"mustn't","explanation":"mustn't = not allowed.","explanation_ar":"mustn't تعني ممنوع."},{"q":"You ___ come early tomorrow. The lesson starts at nine.","options":["must","don't have to","mustn't","has to"],"answer":"don't have to","explanation":"don't have to = not necessary.","explanation_ar":"don't have to تعني غير ضروري."},{"q":"","options":["My sister have to wear a uniform.","My sister has wear a uniform.","My sister must to wear a uniform.","My sister has to wear a uniform."],"answer":"My sister has to wear a uniform.","explanation":"he / she / it → has to / doesn't have to.","explanation_ar":"المفرد الغائب ← has to."},{"q":"","options":["You must washes your hands before lunch.","You must to wash your hands before lunch.","You must wash your hands before lunch.","You musts wash your hands before lunch."],"answer":"You must wash your hands before lunch.","explanation":"No to after must; must has no -s.","explanation_ar":"لا to بعد must."},{"q":"Does your brother have to study tonight? – No, he ___.","options":["hasn't","mustn't","don't","doesn't"],"answer":"doesn't","explanation":"don't have to = not necessary.","explanation_ar":"don't have to تعني غير ضروري."},{"q":"\"Phones are not allowed in the exam.\" = You ___ use phones.","options":["must","mustn't","don't have to","have to"],"answer":"mustn't","explanation":"mustn't = not allowed.","explanation_ar":"mustn't تعني ممنوع."},{"q":"\"It's not necessary to bring a pen. We have pens.\" = You ___ bring a pen.","options":["must","mustn't","don't have to","have to"],"answer":"don't have to","explanation":"don't have to = not necessary.","explanation_ar":"don't have to تعني غير ضروري."},{"q":"Visitors ___ take photos in the museum. Look at the sign!","options":["mustn't","have","don't have to","musts"],"answer":"mustn't","explanation":"mustn't = not allowed.","explanation_ar":"mustn't تعني ممنوع."},{"q":"","options":["Have we to finish this today?","Do we have finish this today?","Do we must finish this today?","Do we have to finish this today?"],"answer":"Do we have to finish this today?","explanation":"he / she / it → has to / doesn't have to.","explanation_ar":"المفرد الغائب ← has to."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Mr. Khalid giving a new student, Adam, a tour of the school, pointing at signs: \"No running\", a uniform poster, a water fountain and the canteen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Mr. Khalid giving a new student, Adam, a tour of the school, pointing at signs: \"No running\", a uniform poster, a water fountain and the canteen"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about must / mustn't / have to / don't have to, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about must / mustn't / have to / don't have to, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows rule (something that tells you what you must or mustn't do); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing rule: something that tells you what you must or mustn't do"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows manners (polite ways of behaving with other people); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing manners: polite ways of behaving with other people"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows polite (showing good manners and respect); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing polite: showing good manners and respect"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows rude (not polite); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing rude: not polite"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Four Corners Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Four Corners Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS1-W01","script":"rule. rule. Our class has five simple rules.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS1-W02","script":"manners. manners. Good manners make everyone feel welcome.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS1-W03","script":"polite. polite. It's polite to say \"please\".","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS1-W04","script":"rude. rude. It's rude to interrupt someone.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS1-T1","script":"Adam is new at our school, so Mr. Khalid is explaining the rules. \"You must wear your uniform every day, and you must arrive before seven o'clock. You mustn't run in the corridors – it's dangerous. You have to bring your own water bottle, but you don't have to bring lunch. The canteen sells healthy food.\" Adam asked, \"Do I have to speak English all day?\" \"No, you don't have to,\" said Mr. Khalid, \"but you should try! And you should ask for help when you need it.\" Adam smiled. \"Thank you. The rules are fair.\"","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “You Must Wear Your Uniform: must, mustn't, have to, don't have to”. Let’s learn must / mustn't / have to / don't have to together. Listen to the start of “Welcome to Our School!”: Adam is new at our school, so Mr. Khalid is explaining the rules. Look at the green words. Use must and have to + base verb for rules and things that are necessary: You must wear a seat belt. I have to get up early. mustn't (must not) = it is not allowed – don't do it! You mustn't run in the hall. Here are some examples. Drivers must stop at a red light. You mustn't touch the paintings in the museum. I have to finish my homework before dinner. Be careful! Some learners say: “You must to wear a helmet.” That’s not right. We say: “You must wear a helmet.” No to after must. Quick check: \"You mustn't swim here.\" Can you swim here? … Think! … No – it's not allowed. Great job! Now you can say: I can explain school rules with must and have to.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS2","title":"You Should Ask for Help: should and shouldn't","objectives":["Students will be able to give advice with should and shouldn't + base verb.","Students will be able to ask for advice with Should I…? and soften advice with I think / I don't think.","I can give advice: \"You should drink more water.\"","I can ask \"Should I tell the teacher?\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تقديم النصيحة باستخدام should وshouldn't + الفعل الأصلي.","سيتمكن الطلاب من طلب النصيحة بـ Should I…? وتلطيفها بـ I think.","أستطيع أن أقدّم نصيحة: You should drink more water.","أستطيع أن أسأل Should I tell the teacher?"],"vocabulary":[{"word":"respect","pos":"noun / verb","ipa":"/rɪˈspɛkt/","definition":"a feeling that someone is important; to show this","arabic":"احترام / يحترم","example":"We respect our teachers and our elders.","image_id":"GV-L04-U3-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS2-W01"},{"word":"safety","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈseɪfti/","definition":"being safe from danger","arabic":"السلامة","example":"Safety comes first in the science lab.","image_id":"GV-L04-U3-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS2-W02"},{"word":"helmet","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhɛlmət/","definition":"a hard hat that protects your head","arabic":"خوذة","example":"Always wear a helmet on your bike.","image_id":"GV-L04-U3-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS2-W03"},{"word":"seat belt","pos":"noun","ipa":"/sit bɛlt/","definition":"a belt in a car that keeps you safe","arabic":"حزام الأمان","example":"Fasten your seat belt before the car moves.","image_id":"GV-L04-U3-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Use should + base verb to give advice (a good idea): You should sleep early. Use shouldn't for a bad idea: You shouldn't eat so much candy.\nshould is softer than must. must = a rule or a strong necessity; should = my advice or opinion.\nAsk for advice: Should I call him? – Yes, you should. / No, you shouldn't. To be polite, say I think you should… or I don't think you should….","examples":["You should wear a helmet when you ride your bike.","You shouldn't talk while your friend is speaking.","Should I invite all my classmates?","I think you should say sorry to your brother.","We shouldn't waste water.","What should I bring to the party?","You should knock before you enter a room.","I don't think you should buy that game."],"common_errors":["✗ You should to sleep early. → ✓ You should sleep early. (No to after should.)","✗ He shoulds eat breakfast. → ✓ He should eat breakfast. (should never takes -s.)","✗ Do I should call him? → ✓ Should I call him? (Question: Should + subject.)","✗ You must eat more vegetables. (friendly advice) → ✓ You should eat more vegetables. (Advice → should (softer).)"],"arabic":"نستخدم should + الفعل الأصلي للنصيحة: You should sleep early، وshouldn't للنهي اللطيف.\nshould أخف من must: must قاعدة أو ضرورة، وshould نصيحة.\nالسؤال: Should I…? (هل يجب أن… / هل من الأفضل أن…؟)، ولا نستخدم do."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “You Should Ask for Help: should and shouldn't”. Let’s learn should / shouldn't for advice; Should I…?; I think you should… together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U3-LS2 | You Should Ask for Help: should and shouldn't","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: You should say sorry. You shouldn't stay up late. Should I wear a jacket? – Yes, you should. • What should I do?","on_screen":"You should say sorry. | You shouldn't stay up late. | Should I wear a jacket? – Yes, you should. • What should I do?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Use should + base verb to give advice (a good idea): You should sleep early. Use shouldn't for a bad idea: You shouldn't eat so much candy. should is softer than must. must = a rule or a strong necessity; should = my advice or opinion.","on_screen":"should / shouldn't for advice; Should I…?; I think you should…","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. You should wear a helmet when you ride your bike. You shouldn't talk while your friend is speaking. Should I invite all my classmates?","on_screen":"You should wear a helmet when you ride your bike. / You shouldn't talk while your friend is speaking. / Should I invite all my classmates?","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “You should to sleep early.” That’s not right. We say: “You should sleep early.” No to after should.","on_screen":"✗ You should to sleep early.   ✓ You should sleep early.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"You should drink more water.\" Is it a rule or advice? … Think! … Advice. Great job! Now you can say: I can give advice: \"You should drink more water.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can give advice: \"You should drink more water.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: should / shouldn't for advice; Should I…?; I think you should….","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم should + الفعل الأصلي للنصيحة: You should sleep early، وshouldn't للنهي اللطيف.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: You should to sleep early. — الصحيح: You should sleep early.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقدّم نصيحة: You should drink more water."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"You look tired. You ___ go to bed early.","options":["mustn't","should to","shouldn't","should"],"answer":"should","explanation":"should + base verb = advice (good idea).","explanation_ar":"should للنصيحة."},{"q":"You ___ eat fast food every day. It's unhealthy.","options":["don't should","should","shouldn't","must"],"answer":"shouldn't","explanation":"shouldn't + base verb = a bad idea.","explanation_ar":"shouldn't للنهي اللطيف."},{"q":"___ I tell my mom about the broken cup?","options":["Should","Am","Must to","Do"],"answer":"Should","explanation":"Should + subject + base verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ Should."},{"q":"He should ___ his room.","options":["tidying","tidies","tidy","to tidy"],"answer":"tidy","explanation":"No to and no -s with should.","explanation_ar":"لا to ولا s مع should."},{"q":"It's cold. – I think you ___ wear a jacket.","options":["don't have","must to","shouldn't","should"],"answer":"should","explanation":"should + base verb = advice (good idea).","explanation_ar":"should للنصيحة."},{"q":"Which is advice, not a rule?","options":["You mustn't smoke here.","You should read every day.","You must wear a seat belt.","You must stop at red lights."],"answer":"You should read every day.","explanation":"should = advice; must = rule.","explanation_ar":"الفرق بين should وmust."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Give advice. Use should or shouldn't.","items":[{"q":"My tooth hurts. (see a dentist)  (advice)","options":[],"answer":"You should see a dentist.","explanation":"should + base verb = advice (good idea).","explanation_ar":"should للنصيحة."},{"q":"I'm always late. (stay up late)  (advice)","options":[],"answer":"You shouldn't stay up late.","explanation":"shouldn't + base verb = a bad idea.","explanation_ar":"shouldn't للنهي اللطيف."},{"q":"I feel thirsty. (drink some water)  (advice)","options":[],"answer":"You should drink some water.","explanation":"should + base verb = advice (good idea).","explanation_ar":"should للنصيحة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make questions with Should I…?","items":[{"q":"I / bring a gift  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Should I bring a gift?","explanation":"Should + subject + base verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ Should."},{"q":"I / call the doctor  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Should I call the doctor?","explanation":"Should + subject + base verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ Should."},{"q":"What / I / say  (question)","options":[],"answer":"What should I say?","explanation":"Should + subject + base verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ Should."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Give advice to these people.","items":[{"q":"Faisal wants to be a good footballer.","options":[],"answer":"He should practice every day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses should / shouldn't for advice; Should I…?; I think you should… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Noura is nervous about her test.","options":[],"answer":"She should study and sleep well.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses should / shouldn't for advice; Should I…?; I think you should… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Rakan is always on his phone.","options":[],"answer":"He shouldn't use his phone so much.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses should / shouldn't for advice; Should I…?; I think you should… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A new student has no friends.","options":[],"answer":"He should join a club.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses should / shouldn't for advice; Should I…?; I think you should… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Your little brother doesn't eat vegetables.","options":[],"answer":"He should try one new vegetable every week.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses should / shouldn't for advice; Should I…?; I think you should… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: \"Ask Zaki\" advice column.","items":[{"q":"Write a short problem letter to Zaki (2 sentences).","options":[],"answer":"Dear Zaki, I forget my homework every day. What should I do?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses should / shouldn't for advice; Should I…?; I think you should… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write Zaki's answer with 3 pieces of advice.","options":[],"answer":"You should write your homework in a planner. You should check your bag at night. You shouldn't leave it until the morning.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses should / shouldn't for advice; Should I…?; I think you should… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one rule (must) and one piece of advice (should) for a school trip.","options":[],"answer":"You must stay with your group. You should bring a hat.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses should / shouldn't for advice; Should I…?; I think you should… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Snakes & Ladders","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Roll and move. If you land on a cue square, make a sentence with the cue and should / shouldn't for advice; Should I…?; I think you should….","Correct at the bottom of a ladder: climb. Incorrect at the head of a snake: slide down.","Teammates are the judges and must explain any correction.","First player to reach square 30 wins."],"data":[{"cue":"wear a seat belt / must"},{"cue":"run in the hall / mustn't"},{"cue":"wear a uniform on Friday / don't have to"},{"cue":"drink water / should"},{"cue":"eat too much candy / shouldn't"},{"cue":"bring a pencil / have to"},{"cue":"shout in the library / mustn't"},{"cue":"say thank you / should"},{"cue":"pay to enter the park / don't have to"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"You have a cold. You ___ drink warm soup.","options":["should to","shouldn't","mustn't","should"],"answer":"should","explanation":"should + base verb = advice (good idea).","explanation_ar":"should للنصيحة."},{"q":"We ___ throw trash on the beach.","options":["shouldn't","don't should","should","must to"],"answer":"shouldn't","explanation":"shouldn't + base verb = a bad idea.","explanation_ar":"shouldn't للنهي اللطيف."},{"q":"","options":["Do I should wear my new thobe?","Should I wear my new thobe?","Should I to wear my new thobe?","I should wear my new thobe?"],"answer":"Should I wear my new thobe?","explanation":"Should + subject + base verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ Should."},{"q":"","options":["She should practices the piano more.","She should practice the piano more.","She should to practice the piano more.","She shoulds practice the piano more."],"answer":"She should practice the piano more.","explanation":"No to and no -s with should.","explanation_ar":"لا to ولا s مع should."},{"q":"What ___ I do? I lost my key.","options":["do","shall to","am","should"],"answer":"should","explanation":"Should + subject + base verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ Should."},{"q":"I don't think you ___ watch that scary film.","options":["should","have","shouldn't","must"],"answer":"should","explanation":"should + base verb = advice (good idea).","explanation_ar":"should للنصيحة."},{"q":"Which sentence is a strong rule?","options":["I think you should rest.","You must stop at the red light.","Maybe you should call him.","You should eat more fruit."],"answer":"You must stop at the red light.","explanation":"should = advice; must = rule.","explanation_ar":"الفرق بين should وmust."},{"q":"","options":["You shouldn't shouts at your sister.","You don't should shout at your sister.","You shouldn't shout at your sister.","You shouldn't to shout at your sister."],"answer":"You shouldn't shout at your sister.","explanation":"shouldn't + base verb = a bad idea.","explanation_ar":"shouldn't للنهي اللطيف."},{"q":"Should I take an umbrella? – Yes, you ___.","options":["must to","do","should","shall"],"answer":"should","explanation":"Should + subject + base verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ Should."},{"q":"Your friend is sad. You ___ talk to him.","options":["mustn't","don't have","shouldn't","should"],"answer":"should","explanation":"should + base verb = advice (good idea).","explanation_ar":"should للنصيحة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"An \"Ask Zaki\" advice corner in the school magazine with letters from students and Zaki the Falcon writing answers with a pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"An \"Ask Zaki\" advice corner in the school magazine with letters from students and Zaki the Falcon writing answers with a pen"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of should / shouldn't for advice; Should I…?; I think you should…: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Rules and Manners”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of should / shouldn't for advice"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows respect (a feeling that someone is important; to show this); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing respect: a feeling that someone is important; to show this"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows safety (being safe from danger); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing safety: being safe from danger"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows helmet (a hard hat that protects your head); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing helmet: a hard hat that protects your head"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows seat belt (a belt in a car that keeps you safe); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing seat belt: a belt in a car that keeps you safe"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Snakes & Ladders”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Snakes & Ladders"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS2-W01","script":"respect. respect. We respect our teachers and our elders.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS2-W02","script":"safety. safety. Safety comes first in the science lab.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS2-W03","script":"helmet. helmet. Always wear a helmet on your bike.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS2-W04","script":"seat belt. seat belt. Fasten your seat belt before the car moves.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “You Should Ask for Help: should and shouldn't”. Let’s learn should / shouldn't for advice; Should I…?; I think you should… together. Remember these patterns: You should say sorry. You shouldn't stay up late. Should I wear a jacket? – Yes, you should. • What should I do? Use should + base verb to give advice (a good idea): You should sleep early. Use shouldn't for a bad idea: You shouldn't eat so much candy. should is softer than must. must = a rule or a strong necessity; should = my advice or opinion. Here are some examples. You should wear a helmet when you ride your bike. You shouldn't talk while your friend is speaking. Should I invite all my classmates? Be careful! Some learners say: “You should to sleep early.” That’s not right. We say: “You should sleep early.” No to after should. Quick check: \"You should drink more water.\" Is it a rule or advice? … Think! … Advice. Great job! Now you can say: I can give advice: \"You should drink more water.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3","title":"Please, Thank You and Safety First: Manners and Safety Words","objectives":["Students will be able to use words about manners, respect and safety.","Students will be able to use collocations for polite and safe behavior.","I can talk about good manners and safety rules.","I can say \"wait in line\", \"take turns\" and \"ask for permission\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام كلمات الآداب والاحترام والسلامة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام المتلازمات اللفظية للسلوك المهذب والآمن.","أستطيع أن أتحدث عن الآداب وقواعد السلامة.","أستطيع أن أقول wait in line وtake turns وask for permission."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"uniform","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈjunəˌfɔrm/","definition":"the special clothes that students or workers wear","arabic":"زي موحد","example":"Our school uniform is a white thobe.","image_id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS3-W01"},{"word":"permission","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pɚˈmɪʃən/","definition":"when someone says you can do something","arabic":"إذن","example":"Ask for permission before you leave the class.","image_id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS3-W02"},{"word":"allowed","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/əˈlaʊd/","definition":"permitted; something you can do","arabic":"مسموح","example":"Phones aren't allowed in the exam room.","image_id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS3-W03"},{"word":"guest","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɡɛst/","definition":"a person you invite to your home","arabic":"ضيف","example":"We serve coffee and dates to our guests.","image_id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS3-W04"},{"word":"line","pos":"noun","ipa":"/laɪn/","definition":"people waiting one behind the other (American English)","arabic":"طابور / صف","example":"Please wait in line at the canteen.","image_id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS3-W05"}],"explanation":{"text":"Manners are polite ways to behave. Polite ↔ rude. We show respect to parents, teachers, elders and guests.\nPolite actions: say please and thank you, wait in line, take turns, knock on the door, ask for permission, welcome guests, shake hands.\nSafety words: safety, helmet, seat belt, allowed, dangerous. In American English we wait in line (British: queue).\nCollocations/phrases: say please / thank you / sorry • wait in line • take turns • knock on the door | ask for permission • welcome a guest • show respect • keep your promise | wear a helmet / a seat belt • follow the rules • be careful • stay safe","examples":["It's polite to knock on the door before you go in.","Interrupting people is rude.","We show respect to our grandparents.","Please wait in line for your turn.","You must ask for permission to leave the class.","Fasten your seat belt, please.","Phones aren't allowed in the exam.","We serve Arabic coffee to every guest."],"common_errors":["✗ Please stay in the queue. (American English) → ✓ Please wait in line. (In American English, use line.)","✗ He is very rude boy. → ✓ He is a very rude boy. (Don't forget a.)","✗ I took permission from my teacher. → ✓ I asked for permission / I got permission. (ask for permission.)","✗ Wear your belt in the car. → ✓ Wear your seat belt in the car. (seat belt is the safety belt.)"],"arabic":"الآداب: polite (مهذب) ↔ rude (وقح)، وrespect (احترام).\nسلوكيات مهذبة: wait in line (انتظر في الطابور)، take turns (تبادل الأدوار)، ask for permission (اطلب الإذن).\nكلمات السلامة: helmet (خوذة) وseat belt (حزام الأمان) وallowed (مسموح).\nنقول ask for permission وليس take permission."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Please, Thank You and Safety First: Manners and Safety Words”. Let’s learn manners and safety vocabulary; polite ↔ rude; collocations (wait in line, take turns, ask for permission, wear a helmet) together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U3-LS3 | Please, Thank You and Safety First: Manners and Safety Words","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. uniform: the special clothes that students or workers wear. permission: when someone says you can do something. allowed: permitted; something you can do.","on_screen":"uniform | permission | allowed","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Manners are polite ways to behave. Polite ↔ rude. We show respect to parents, teachers, elders and guests. Polite actions: say please and thank you, wait in line, take turns, knock on the door, ask for permission, welcome guests, shake hands.","on_screen":"manners and safety vocabulary; polite ↔ rude; collocations (wait in line, take turns, ask for permission, wear a helmet)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. It's polite to knock on the door before you go in. Interrupting people is rude. We show respect to our grandparents.","on_screen":"It's polite to knock on the door before you go in. / Interrupting people is rude. / We show respect to our grandparents.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Please stay in the queue. (American English).” That’s not right. We say: “Please wait in line.” In American English, use line.","on_screen":"✗ Please stay in the queue. (American English)   ✓ Please wait in line.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Is it polite or rude to push in front of people? … Think! … Rude. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about good manners and safety rules.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can talk about good manners and safety rules.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: manners and safety vocabulary; polite ↔ rude; collocations (wait in line, take turns, ask for permission, wear a helmet).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الآداب: polite (مهذب) ↔ rude (وقح)، وrespect (احترام).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Please stay in the queue. (American English) — الصحيح: Please wait in line.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أتحدث عن الآداب وقواعد السلامة."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"Saying \"thank you\" is ___.","options":["polite","allowed","rude","dangerous"],"answer":"polite","explanation":"polite ↔ rude.","explanation_ar":"مهذب ↔ وقح."},{"q":"Please ___ in line at the canteen.","options":["make","stand up","take","wait"],"answer":"wait","explanation":"American English: wait in line.","explanation_ar":"الإنجليزية الأمريكية: wait in line."},{"q":"In the game, we ___ turns.","options":["take","make","have","do"],"answer":"take","explanation":"Use the right manners or safety collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Always wear a ___ when you ride a bike.","options":["guest","uniform","helmet","seat belt"],"answer":"helmet","explanation":"Choose the safety word that fits.","explanation_ar":"كلمة السلامة المناسبة."},{"q":"You must ___ permission before you use the computer.","options":["make","ask for","take","do"],"answer":"ask for","explanation":"Use the right manners or safety collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Talking with food in your mouth is ___.","options":["polite","rude","allowed","respectful"],"answer":"rude","explanation":"polite ↔ rude.","explanation_ar":"مهذب ↔ وقح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the situation to the polite action.","items":[{"q":"Before you enter a room","options":["welcome him and serve coffee","say thank you","ask for permission","wait in line","knock on the door","take turns"],"answer":"knock on the door","explanation":"Before you enter a room → knock on the door. polite ↔ rude.","explanation_ar":"مهذب ↔ وقح."},{"q":"When someone gives you a gift","options":["welcome him and serve coffee","say thank you","ask for permission","wait in line","knock on the door","take turns"],"answer":"say thank you","explanation":"When someone gives you a gift → say thank you. polite ↔ rude.","explanation_ar":"مهذب ↔ وقح."},{"q":"When you want to borrow something","options":["welcome him and serve coffee","say thank you","ask for permission","wait in line","knock on the door","take turns"],"answer":"ask for permission","explanation":"When you want to borrow something → ask for permission. polite ↔ rude.","explanation_ar":"مهذب ↔ وقح."},{"q":"When a guest arrives","options":["welcome him and serve coffee","say thank you","ask for permission","wait in line","knock on the door","take turns"],"answer":"welcome him and serve coffee","explanation":"When a guest arrives → welcome him and serve coffee. polite ↔ rude.","explanation_ar":"مهذب ↔ وقح."},{"q":"At the bus stop","options":["welcome him and serve coffee","say thank you","ask for permission","wait in line","knock on the door","take turns"],"answer":"wait in line","explanation":"At the bus stop → wait in line. polite ↔ rude.","explanation_ar":"مهذب ↔ وقح."},{"q":"In a game with friends","options":["welcome him and serve coffee","say thank you","ask for permission","wait in line","knock on the door","take turns"],"answer":"take turns","explanation":"In a game with friends → take turns. polite ↔ rude.","explanation_ar":"مهذب ↔ وقح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about manners in your home and school.","items":[{"q":"In my family, it's polite to ___.","options":[],"answer":"In my family, it's polite to greet the elders first.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses manners and safety vocabulary; polite ↔ rude; collocations (wait in line, take turns, ask for permission, wear a helmet) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In my school, it's rude to ___.","options":[],"answer":"In my school, it's rude to interrupt the teacher.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses manners and safety vocabulary; polite ↔ rude; collocations (wait in line, take turns, ask for permission, wear a helmet) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I show respect to ___ by ___.","options":[],"answer":"I show respect to my grandpa by kissing his head.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses manners and safety vocabulary; polite ↔ rude; collocations (wait in line, take turns, ask for permission, wear a helmet) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"When guests visit us, we ___.","options":[],"answer":"When guests visit us, we serve coffee and dates.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses manners and safety vocabulary; polite ↔ rude; collocations (wait in line, take turns, ask for permission, wear a helmet) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A safety rule in our car is ___.","options":[],"answer":"A safety rule in our car is \"Everyone wears a seat belt.\"","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses manners and safety vocabulary; polite ↔ rude; collocations (wait in line, take turns, ask for permission, wear a helmet) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Make a \"Good Manners\" comic.","items":[{"q":"Draw 4 boxes. Write one polite action in each box.","options":[],"answer":"say please, wait in line, knock on the door, take turns","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses manners and safety vocabulary; polite ↔ rude; collocations (wait in line, take turns, ask for permission, wear a helmet) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about good manners with should.","options":[],"answer":"You should say thank you. You should wait in line. You shouldn't push.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses manners and safety vocabulary; polite ↔ rude; collocations (wait in line, take turns, ask for permission, wear a helmet) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one safety sentence with allowed.","options":[],"answer":"Running is not allowed near the pool.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses manners and safety vocabulary; polite ↔ rude; collocations (wait in line, take turns, ask for permission, wear a helmet) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Dominoes","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Deal the dominoes equally in teams of four.","Player 1 places a domino; the next player adds a domino whose word matches the open definition.","If you cannot play, pass.","The first player with no dominoes left wins."],"data":[{"word":"rule","match":"something that tells you what you must or mustn't do","arabic":"قاعدة / قانون"},{"word":"manners","match":"polite ways of behaving with other people","arabic":"آداب / سلوك مهذب"},{"word":"polite","match":"showing good manners and respect","arabic":"مهذب"},{"word":"rude","match":"not polite","arabic":"وقح / غير مهذب"},{"word":"respect","match":"a feeling that someone is important; to show this","arabic":"احترام / يحترم"},{"word":"safety","match":"being safe from danger","arabic":"السلامة"},{"word":"helmet","match":"a hard hat that protects your head","arabic":"خوذة"},{"word":"seat belt","match":"a belt in a car that keeps you safe","arabic":"حزام الأمان"},{"word":"uniform","match":"the special clothes that students or workers wear","arabic":"زي موحد"},{"word":"permission","match":"when someone says you can do something","arabic":"إذن"},{"word":"allowed","match":"permitted; something you can do","arabic":"مسموح"},{"word":"guest","match":"a person you invite to your home","arabic":"ضيف"},{"word":"line","match":"people waiting one behind the other (American English)","arabic":"طابور / صف"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Pushing in front of people is ___.","options":["allowed","respectful","polite","rude"],"answer":"rude","explanation":"polite ↔ rude.","explanation_ar":"مهذب ↔ وقح."},{"q":"Fasten your ___ before the plane takes off.","options":["line","seat belt","helmet","uniform"],"answer":"seat belt","explanation":"Choose the safety word that fits.","explanation_ar":"كلمة السلامة المناسبة."},{"q":"We ___ respect to our teachers.","options":["do","make","show","take"],"answer":"show","explanation":"Use the right manners or safety collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"You must ___ on the door before you come in.","options":["knock","wait","push","hit"],"answer":"knock","explanation":"Use the right manners or safety collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Phones are not ___ in the mosque during prayer.","options":["polite","rude","safety","allowed"],"answer":"allowed","explanation":"Choose the safety word that fits.","explanation_ar":"كلمة السلامة المناسبة."},{"q":"In American English, people wait ___.","options":["in line","at line","in row","in queue"],"answer":"in line","explanation":"American English: wait in line.","explanation_ar":"الإنجليزية الأمريكية: wait in line."},{"q":"We serve dates and coffee to our ___.","options":["rules","uniforms","guests","helmets"],"answer":"guests","explanation":"Use the right manners or safety collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Students wear the same clothes at school. It's a ___.","options":["seat belt","uniform","helmet","permission"],"answer":"uniform","explanation":"Choose the safety word that fits.","explanation_ar":"كلمة السلامة المناسبة."},{"q":"Good ___ means behaving politely.","options":["safety","manners","permission","uniform"],"answer":"manners","explanation":"Use the right manners or safety collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Which action is polite?","options":["saying \"Excuse me\"","pushing in line","shouting in class","taking without asking"],"answer":"saying \"Excuse me\"","explanation":"polite ↔ rude.","explanation_ar":"مهذب ↔ وقح."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A collage of good manners and safety: students waiting in line at the canteen, a boy knocking on a door, a girl in a bike helmet, a family wearing seat belts and a host serving dates to a guest. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A collage of good manners and safety: students waiting in line at the canteen, a boy knocking on a door, a girl in a bike helmet, a family wearing seat belts and a host serving dates to a guest"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows uniform (the special clothes that students or workers wear); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing uniform: the special clothes that students or workers wear"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows permission (when someone says you can do something); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing permission: when someone says you can do something"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows allowed (permitted; something you can do); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing allowed: permitted; something you can do"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows guest (a person you invite to your home); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing guest: a person you invite to your home"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows line (people waiting one behind the other (American English)); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing line: people waiting one behind the other (American English)"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Dominoes”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Dominoes"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS3-W01","script":"uniform. uniform. Our school uniform is a white thobe.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS3-W02","script":"permission. permission. Ask for permission before you leave the class.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS3-W03","script":"allowed. allowed. Phones aren't allowed in the exam room.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS3-W04","script":"guest. guest. We serve coffee and dates to our guests.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS3-W05","script":"line. line. Please wait in line at the canteen.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Please, Thank You and Safety First: Manners and Safety Words”. Let’s learn manners and safety vocabulary; polite ↔ rude; collocations (wait in line, take turns, ask for permission, wear a helmet) together. Meet some new words. uniform: the special clothes that students or workers wear. permission: when someone says you can do something. allowed: permitted; something you can do. Manners are polite ways to behave. Polite ↔ rude. We show respect to parents, teachers, elders and guests. Polite actions: say please and thank you, wait in line, take turns, knock on the door, ask for permission, welcome guests, shake hands. Here are some examples. It's polite to knock on the door before you go in. Interrupting people is rude. We show respect to our grandparents. Be careful! Some learners say: “Please stay in the queue. (American English).” That’s not right. We say: “Please wait in line.” In American English, use line. Quick check: Is it polite or rude to push in front of people? … Think! … Rude. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about good manners and safety rules.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS4","title":"The Teacher's Desk and the Teachers' Room: Possessive Apostrophes","objectives":["Students will be able to show possession with 's for singular nouns and s' for regular plural nouns.","Students will be able to use 's with irregular plurals (children's, men's, women's).","I can write \"the boy's bag\" and \"the boys' bags\".","I can write \"the children's playground\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التعبير عن الملكية بـ 's للمفرد وs' للجمع المنتظم.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام 's مع الجموع الشاذة (children's وmen's وwomen's).","أستطيع أن أكتب the boy's bag وthe boys' bags.","أستطيع أن أكتب the children's playground."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"rule","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rul/","definition":"something that tells you what you must or mustn't do","arabic":"قاعدة / قانون","example":"Our class has five simple rules.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"manners","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmænɚz/","definition":"polite ways of behaving with other people","arabic":"آداب / سلوك مهذب","example":"Good manners make everyone feel welcome.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"polite","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/pəˈlaɪt/","definition":"showing good manners and respect","arabic":"مهذب","example":"It's polite to say \"please\".","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"rude","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/rud/","definition":"not polite","arabic":"وقح / غير مهذب","example":"It's rude to interrupt someone.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"respect","pos":"noun / verb","ipa":"/rɪˈspɛkt/","definition":"a feeling that someone is important; to show this","arabic":"احترام / يحترم","example":"We respect our teachers and our elders.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"safety","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈseɪfti/","definition":"being safe from danger","arabic":"السلامة","example":"Safety comes first in the science lab.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"For one owner, add 's: the teacher's desk (one teacher), Lina's camera.\nFor a plural owner ending in -s, add only an apostrophe after the s: the teachers' room (many teachers), my parents' car.\nFor irregular plurals that don't end in -s, add 's: the children's toys, the men's prayer area, the women's section.\none owner → 's: my brother's room\nplural owner ending in -s → s': my brothers' room (two or more brothers)\nirregular plural → 's: children's, men's, women's, people's\nDon't use an apostrophe for a simple plural: two books (NOT two book's)","examples":["This is the principal's office.","The girls' uniforms are dark blue.","The children's library is upstairs.","My grandparents' house has a big garden.","Yusuf's helmet is green.","The students' work is on the wall.","Where is the men's bathroom?","The nurse's badge has her name on it."],"common_errors":["✗ My parent's car is new. (two parents) → ✓ My parents' car is new. (Plural owner → s'.)","✗ The childrens' room → ✓ The children's room (children is irregular → 's.)","✗ I have three cat's. → ✓ I have three cats. (A simple plural has no apostrophe.)","✗ The boy bag is here. → ✓ The boy's bag is here. (Show possession with 's.)"],"arabic":"للمالك المفرد نضيف 's: the teacher's desk (مكتب المعلم).\nللمالك الجمع المنتهي بـ s نضيف ' فقط: the teachers' room (غرفة المعلمين).\nللجمع الشاذ نضيف 's: the children's toys (ألعاب الأطفال).\nلا نضع فاصلة علوية في الجمع العادي: three cats."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Teacher's Desk and the Teachers' Room: Possessive Apostrophes”. Let’s learn possessive apostrophes: singular 's, plural s', irregular plural 's (children's) together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U3-LS4 | The Teacher's Desk and the Teachers' Room: Possessive Apostrophes","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"For one owner, add 's: the teacher's desk (one teacher), Lina's camera.","on_screen":"possessive apostrophes: singular 's, plural s', irregular plural 's (children's)","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"For one owner, add 's: the teacher's desk (one teacher), Lina's camera. For a plural owner ending in -s, add only an apostrophe after the s: the teachers' room (many teachers), my parents' car.","on_screen":"one owner → 's: my brother's room • plural owner ending in -s → s': my brothers' room (two or more brothers) • irregular plural → 's: children's, men's, women's, people's","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. This is the principal's office. The girls' uniforms are dark blue. The children's library is upstairs.","on_screen":"This is the principal's office. / The girls' uniforms are dark blue. / The children's library is upstairs.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “My parent's car is new. (two parents).” That’s not right. We say: “My parents' car is new.” Plural owner → s'.","on_screen":"✗ My parent's car is new. (two parents)   ✓ My parents' car is new.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"the boys' bags\" – one boy or many boys? … Think! … Many boys. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"the boy's bag\" and \"the boys' bags\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"the boy's bag\" and \"the boys' bags\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: possessive apostrophes: singular 's, plural s', irregular plural 's (children's).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","للمالك المفرد نضيف 's: the teacher's desk (مكتب المعلم).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: My parent's car is new. (two parents) — الصحيح: My parents' car is new.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب the boy's bag وthe boys' bags."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"School Notice (editing passage)","body":"Welcome to the students art show! You can see the childrens paintings in the hall. Mr. Khalids class made the posters. Please don't touch the painting's. The parents meeting is at five.","word_count":32,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct form.","items":[{"q":"This is my ___ room. (one sister)","options":["sisters","sisters'","sister's","sister"],"answer":"sister's","explanation":"One owner → 's.","explanation_ar":"المالك المفرد ← 's."},{"q":"The ___ classroom is on the first floor. (many boys)","options":["boys'","boys","boy's","boys's"],"answer":"boys'","explanation":"Plural owner ending in -s → s'.","explanation_ar":"المالك الجمع ← s'."},{"q":"The ___ park has new swings.","options":["childrens","children's","childrens'","children'"],"answer":"children's","explanation":"Irregular plural (children, men, women) → 's.","explanation_ar":"الجمع الشاذ ← 's."},{"q":"I have two ___.","options":["brothers'","brother","brothers","brother's"],"answer":"brothers","explanation":"A simple plural has no apostrophe.","explanation_ar":"الجمع العادي بلا فاصلة علوية."},{"q":"My ___ car is white. (Mom and Dad)","options":["parent's","parents'","parents's","parents"],"answer":"parents'","explanation":"Plural owner ending in -s → s'.","explanation_ar":"المالك الجمع ← s'."},{"q":"The ___ prayer room is on the left.","options":["men'","mens","mens'","men's"],"answer":"men's","explanation":"Irregular plural (children, men, women) → 's.","explanation_ar":"الجمع الشاذ ← 's."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the apostrophe.","items":[{"q":"The teacher car is outside.","options":[],"answer":"The teacher's car is outside.","explanation":"teacher → teacher's. One owner → 's.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: teacher → teacher's. المالك المفرد ← 's."},{"q":"The players shirts are green.","options":[],"answer":"The players' shirts are green.","explanation":"players → players'. Plural owner ending in -s → s'.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: players → players'. المالك الجمع ← s'."},{"q":"The womens' section is upstairs.","options":[],"answer":"The women's section is upstairs.","explanation":"womens' → women's. Irregular plural (children, men, women) → 's.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: womens' → women's. الجمع الشاذ ← 's."},{"q":"I bought five pencil's.","options":[],"answer":"I bought five pencils.","explanation":"pencil's → pencils. A simple plural has no apostrophe.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: pencil's → pencils. الجمع العادي بلا فاصلة علوية."},{"q":"Omars bike is new.","options":[],"answer":"Omar's bike is new.","explanation":"Omars → Omar's. One owner → 's.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Omars → Omar's. المالك المفرد ← 's."},{"q":"My cousin's house is in Abha. (all my cousins live there)","options":[],"answer":"My cousins' house is in Abha. (all my cousins live there)","explanation":"cousin's → cousins'. Plural owner ending in -s → s'.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: cousin's → cousins'. المالك الجمع ← s'."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the school notice.","items":[{"q":"Welcome to the students art show!","options":[],"answer":"Welcome to the students' art show!","explanation":"students → students'. One owner → 's.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: students → students'. المالك المفرد ← 's."},{"q":"You can see the childrens paintings in the hall. [Mr.","options":[],"answer":"You can see the children's paintings in the hall. [Mr.","explanation":"childrens → children's. One owner → 's.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: childrens → children's. المالك المفرد ← 's."},{"q":"Mr. Khalids","options":[],"answer":"Mr. Khalid's","explanation":"Mr. Khalids → Mr. Khalid's. One owner → 's.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Mr. Khalids → Mr. Khalid's. المالك المفرد ← 's."},{"q":"Please don't touch the painting's.","options":[],"answer":"Please don't touch the paintings.","explanation":"painting's → paintings. One owner → 's.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: painting's → paintings. المالك المفرد ← 's."},{"q":"The parents meeting is at five.","options":[],"answer":"The parents' meeting is at five.","explanation":"parents → parents'. One owner → 's.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: parents → parents'. المالك المفرد ← 's."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write about your school and family.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 sentences with 's (one owner).","options":[],"answer":"My dad's office is big. Sara's cat is white.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive apostrophes: singular 's, plural s', irregular plural 's (children's) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with s' (many owners).","options":[],"answer":"The teachers' room is quiet. My grandparents' garden is green.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive apostrophes: singular 's, plural s', irregular plural 's (children's) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with children's, men's or women's.","options":[],"answer":"The children's library has comfortable chairs.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive apostrophes: singular 's, plural s', irregular plural 's (children's) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Speed Spell","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a word and a short sentence with it.","Students write the word in 10 seconds.","Show boards on \"Show me!\". Correct = 1 point.","After 10 words, partners check each other's boards and correct any mistakes."],"data":[{"word":"rule","clue":"something that tells you what you must or mustn't do"},{"word":"manners","clue":"polite ways of behaving with other people"},{"word":"polite","clue":"showing good manners and respect"},{"word":"permission","clue":"when someone says you can do something"},{"word":"uniform","clue":"the special clothes that students or workers wear"},{"word":"guest","clue":"a person you invite to your home"},{"word":"rude","clue":"not polite"},{"word":"respect","clue":"a feeling that someone is important; to show this"},{"word":"safety","clue":"being safe from danger"},{"word":"helmet","clue":"a hard hat that protects your head"},{"word":"allowed","clue":"permitted; something you can do"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"This is the ___ desk. (one doctor)","options":["doctors","doctor's","doctors'","doctor"],"answer":"doctor's","explanation":"One owner → 's.","explanation_ar":"المالك المفرد ← 's."},{"q":"The ___ lockers are blue. (many students)","options":["student's","students's","students","students'"],"answer":"students'","explanation":"Plural owner ending in -s → s'.","explanation_ar":"المالك الجمع ← s'."},{"q":"","options":["The childrens playground is new.","The children' playground is new.","The children's playground is new.","The childrens' playground is new."],"answer":"The children's playground is new.","explanation":"Irregular plural (children, men, women) → 's.","explanation_ar":"الجمع الشاذ ← 's."},{"q":"","options":["We have four bikes's.","We have four bikes'.","We have four bikes.","We have four bike's."],"answer":"We have four bikes.","explanation":"A simple plural has no apostrophe.","explanation_ar":"الجمع العادي بلا فاصلة علوية."},{"q":"","options":["My uncle's house is near the sea.","My uncles house is near the sea.","My uncles's house is near the sea.","My uncle house is near the sea."],"answer":"My uncle's house is near the sea.","explanation":"One owner → 's.","explanation_ar":"المالك المفرد ← 's."},{"q":"","options":["The girls' team won the match. (many girls)","The girl's team won the match.","The girls team won the match.","The girls's team won the match."],"answer":"The girls' team won the match. (many girls)","explanation":"Plural owner ending in -s → s'.","explanation_ar":"المالك الجمع ← s'."},{"q":"Which is correct?","options":["the peoples choice","the people' choice","the people's choice","the peoples' choice"],"answer":"the people's choice","explanation":"Irregular plural (children, men, women) → 's.","explanation_ar":"الجمع الشاذ ← 's."},{"q":"","options":["Where are the teachers' books? (many teachers)","Where are the teacher's books?","Where are the teachers books?","Where are the teachers's books?"],"answer":"Where are the teachers' books? (many teachers)","explanation":"Plural owner ending in -s → s'.","explanation_ar":"المالك الجمع ← s'."},{"q":"","options":["Hamad helmet is red.","Hamad's helmet is red.","Hamads helmet is red.","Hamads' helmet is red."],"answer":"Hamad's helmet is red.","explanation":"One owner → 's.","explanation_ar":"المالك المفرد ← 's."},{"q":"Which needs an apostrophe?","options":["guests arrive","many guests came","three guests","the guests coats"],"answer":"the guests coats","explanation":"Plural owner ending in -s → s'.","explanation_ar":"المالك الجمع ← s'."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Rules and Manners” that shows possessive apostrophes: singular 's, plural s', irregular plural 's (children's) in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Rules and Manners” that shows possessive apostrophes: singular 's, plural s', irregular plural 's (children's) in action"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Speed Spell”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Speed Spell"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Teacher's Desk and the Teachers' Room: Possessive Apostrophes”. Let’s learn possessive apostrophes: singular 's, plural s', irregular plural 's (children's) together. For one owner, add 's: the teacher's desk (one teacher), Lina's camera. For one owner, add 's: the teacher's desk (one teacher), Lina's camera. For a plural owner ending in -s, add only an apostrophe after the s: the teachers' room (many teachers), my parents' car. Here are some examples. This is the principal's office. The girls' uniforms are dark blue. The children's library is upstairs. Be careful! Some learners say: “My parent's car is new. (two parents).” That’s not right. We say: “My parents' car is new.” Plural owner → s'. Quick check: \"the boys' bags\" – one boy or many boys? … Think! … Many boys. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"the boy's bag\" and \"the boys' bags\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS5","title":"A Guide to Good Manners: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to discuss rules and give advice to a new student.","Students will be able to write a short guide to good manners with rules, advice and correct possessives.","I can explain rules and give advice to a new student.","I can write a guide to good manners."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من مناقشة القواعد وتقديم النصائح لطالب جديد.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة دليل قصير للآداب الحسنة بالقواعد والنصائح والملكية الصحيحة.","أستطيع أن أشرح القواعد وأقدّم النصائح لطالب جديد.","أستطيع أن أكتب دليلًا للآداب الحسنة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"rule","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rul/","definition":"something that tells you what you must or mustn't do","arabic":"قاعدة / قانون","example":"Our class has five simple rules.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"manners","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmænɚz/","definition":"polite ways of behaving with other people","arabic":"آداب / سلوك مهذب","example":"Good manners make everyone feel welcome.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"polite","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/pəˈlaɪt/","definition":"showing good manners and respect","arabic":"مهذب","example":"It's polite to say \"please\".","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"rude","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/rud/","definition":"not polite","arabic":"وقح / غير مهذب","example":"It's rude to interrupt someone.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"respect","pos":"noun / verb","ipa":"/rɪˈspɛkt/","definition":"a feeling that someone is important; to show this","arabic":"احترام / يحترم","example":"We respect our teachers and our elders.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"safety","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈseɪfti/","definition":"being safe from danger","arabic":"السلامة","example":"Safety comes first in the science lab.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"helmet","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhɛlmət/","definition":"a hard hat that protects your head","arabic":"خوذة","example":"Always wear a helmet on your bike.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"seat belt","pos":"noun","ipa":"/sit bɛlt/","definition":"a belt in a car that keeps you safe","arabic":"حزام الأمان","example":"Fasten your seat belt before the car moves.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"uniform","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈjunəˌfɔrm/","definition":"the special clothes that students or workers wear","arabic":"زي موحد","example":"Our school uniform is a white thobe.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"permission","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pɚˈmɪʃən/","definition":"when someone says you can do something","arabic":"إذن","example":"Ask for permission before you leave the class.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"allowed","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/əˈlaʊd/","definition":"permitted; something you can do","arabic":"مسموح","example":"Phones aren't allowed in the exam room.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"guest","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɡɛst/","definition":"a person you invite to your home","arabic":"ضيف","example":"We serve coffee and dates to our guests.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"line","pos":"noun","ipa":"/laɪn/","definition":"people waiting one behind the other (American English)","arabic":"طابور / صف","example":"Please wait in line at the canteen.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 3: must/mustn't, have to/don't have to, should/shouldn't, manners and safety words, and possessive apostrophes.\nA guide gives clear rules (must) and friendly tips (should). It speaks to the reader as you.\n✔ must / mustn't for rules; don't have to = not necessary\n✔ should / shouldn't for advice\n✔ manners words: polite, respect, permission, wait in line\n✔ possessives: the school's canteen, the students' lockers, the children's library","examples":["You must wear the school's uniform.","You mustn't run in the corridors.","You don't have to buy books – the school gives them.","You should say good morning to the guard.","You shouldn't be late for the bus.","Put your bag in the students' lockers.","Always ask for permission before you leave.","The teachers' room is next to the library."],"common_errors":["✗ You must to wear a uniform. → ✓ You must wear a uniform. (No to after must.)","✗ You mustn't bring lunch – the canteen has food. → ✓ You don't have to bring lunch. (Not necessary → don't have to.)","✗ Don't use other student's things. (many students) → ✓ Don't use other students' things. (Plural owner → s'.)"],"arabic":"نراجع must وmustn't وhave to وdon't have to وshould وكلمات الآداب والملكية.\nالدليل يقدّم قواعد واضحة (must) ونصائح ودية (should) ويخاطب القارئ بـ you.\nتذكّر الفرق بين mustn't (ممنوع) وdon't have to (غير ضروري)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Guide to Good Manners: Language in Use”. Let’s learn must/mustn't/have to/don't have to, should, manners and safety words, possessive apostrophes (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U3-LS5 | A Guide to Good Manners: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Welcome team: one student is a new student from another country. The welcome team explains 3 rules (must/mustn't), 2 things he doesn't have to do and gives 2 pieces of advice (should).","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 3: must/mustn't, have to/don't have to, should/shouldn't, manners and safety words, and possessive apostrophes. A guide gives clear rules (must) and friendly tips (should). It speaks to the reader as you.","on_screen":"✔ must / mustn't for rules; don't have to = not necessary • ✔ should / shouldn't for advice • ✔ manners words: polite, respect, permission, wait in line","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. You must wear the school's uniform. You mustn't run in the corridors. You don't have to buy books – the school gives them.","on_screen":"You must wear the school's uniform. / You mustn't run in the corridors. / You don't have to buy books – the school gives them.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “You must to wear a uniform.” That’s not right. We say: “You must wear a uniform.” No to after must.","on_screen":"✗ You must to wear a uniform.   ✓ You must wear a uniform.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “You mustn't bring lunch – the canteen has food.”? … Think! … It should be “You don't have to bring lunch.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can explain rules and give advice to a new student.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can explain rules and give advice to a new student.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: must/mustn't/have to/don't have to, should, manners and safety words, possessive apostrophes (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع must وmustn't وhave to وdon't have to وshould وكلمات الآداب والملكية.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: You must to wear a uniform. — الصحيح: You must wear a uniform.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أشرح القواعد وأقدّم النصائح لطالب جديد."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"A Guide to Good Manners – Class 4A","body":"Welcome to our school! Here are some tips from Class 4A.\nYou must greet the teachers when you enter the classroom, and you mustn't interrupt them.\nYou don't have to bring lunch – the school's canteen has healthy food.\nYou should wait in line at the canteen and say thank you.\nYou shouldn't use other students' things without permission.\nFinally, you should visit the children's library. It's the best place in the school!","word_count":73,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the guide. True or False?","items":[{"q":"You must greet the teachers when you enter the classroom.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Guide to Good Manners – Class 4A”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"You have to bring your own lunch.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “A Guide to Good Manners – Class 4A”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The school's canteen has healthy food.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Guide to Good Manners – Class 4A”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"You should wait in line at the canteen.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Guide to Good Manners – Class 4A”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"You can use other students' things without permission.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “A Guide to Good Manners – Class 4A”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Class 4A thinks the children's library is the best place in the school.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Guide to Good Manners – Class 4A”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"You ___ interrupt the teacher. It's rude.","options":["have","mustn't","must","don't have to"],"answer":"mustn't","explanation":"must / mustn't for rules.","explanation_ar":"القواعد."},{"q":"You ___ bring lunch. The canteen sells food.","options":["must","don't have to","has to","mustn't"],"answer":"don't have to","explanation":"don't have to = not necessary.","explanation_ar":"غير ضروري."},{"q":"You ___ say thank you. It's polite.","options":["should to","mustn't","should","shouldn't"],"answer":"should","explanation":"should / shouldn't for advice.","explanation_ar":"النصيحة."},{"q":"You should ___ in line at the canteen.","options":["wait","make","stay up","take"],"answer":"wait","explanation":"Manners or safety word.","explanation_ar":"كلمة الآداب."},{"q":"Don't use other ___ things without permission.","options":["student's","students's","students","students'"],"answer":"students'","explanation":"Possessive apostrophe ('s / s').","explanation_ar":"الملكية."},{"q":"Visit the ___ library – it's fantastic!","options":["childrens","children'","children's","childrens'"],"answer":"children's","explanation":"Possessive apostrophe ('s / s').","explanation_ar":"الملكية."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Welcome team. Write what you tell the new student.","items":[{"q":"Rule 1 (must): ___","options":[],"answer":"You must wear the school uniform.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must/mustn't/have to/don't have to, should, manners and safety words, possessive apostrophes (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Rule 2 (mustn't): ___","options":[],"answer":"You mustn't use your phone in class.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must/mustn't/have to/don't have to, should, manners and safety words, possessive apostrophes (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Not necessary (don't have to): ___","options":[],"answer":"You don't have to bring a lot of books.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must/mustn't/have to/don't have to, should, manners and safety words, possessive apostrophes (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Advice 1 (should): ___","options":[],"answer":"You should join the football team.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must/mustn't/have to/don't have to, should, manners and safety words, possessive apostrophes (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Advice 2 (shouldn't): ___","options":[],"answer":"You shouldn't be shy – ask questions!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must/mustn't/have to/don't have to, should, manners and safety words, possessive apostrophes (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your guide.","items":[{"q":"Plan: 2 rules, 1 not necessary, 2 tips, 2 places with possessives.","options":[],"answer":"must arrive on time, mustn't run; don't have to bring water; should join a club, shouldn't be late; teachers' room, school's garden","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must/mustn't/have to/don't have to, should, manners and safety words, possessive apostrophes (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your guide in 6–7 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Welcome to our school! You must arrive before seven. You mustn't run in the halls. You don't have to bring water – the school has fountains. You should join a club. You shouldn't be late for the bus. Visit the school's garden – it's beautiful!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must/mustn't/have to/don't have to, should, manners and safety words, possessive apostrophes (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: must/should without \"to\"? mustn't vs don't have to? apostrophes? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"student's lockers\" to \"students' lockers\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must/mustn't/have to/don't have to, should, manners and safety words, possessive apostrophes (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin the Review Wheel","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["A player spins the wheel and lands on a word.","Say what the word means and use it in a sentence with must/mustn't/have to/don't have to, should, manners and safety words, possessive apostrophes (unit review).","Teammates check: meaning (1 point), grammar (1 point), pronunciation (1 point).","Highest total after 6 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"rule","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"manners","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"polite","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"rude","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"respect","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"safety","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"helmet","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"seat belt","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"uniform","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"permission","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"allowed","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"guest","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"line","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Drivers ___ stop when the light is red.","options":["should to","don't have to","musts","must"],"answer":"must","explanation":"must / mustn't for rules.","explanation_ar":"القواعد."},{"q":"It's a holiday tomorrow. We ___ go to school.","options":["must","have","don't have to","mustn't"],"answer":"don't have to","explanation":"don't have to = not necessary.","explanation_ar":"غير ضروري."},{"q":"You look tired. I think you ___ rest.","options":["mustn't","shouldn't","should to","should"],"answer":"should","explanation":"should / shouldn't for advice.","explanation_ar":"النصيحة."},{"q":"We must ___ for permission to use the lab.","options":["take","ask","make","do"],"answer":"ask","explanation":"Manners or safety word.","explanation_ar":"كلمة الآداب."},{"q":"","options":["The players bags are in the locker room.","The players's bags are in the locker room.","The players' bags are in the locker room. (many players)","The player's bags are in the locker room."],"answer":"The players' bags are in the locker room. (many players)","explanation":"Possessive apostrophe ('s / s').","explanation_ar":"الملكية."},{"q":"","options":["You mustn't eats in the library.","You mustn't eat in the library.","You must not to eat in the library.","You don't must eat in the library."],"answer":"You mustn't eat in the library.","explanation":"must / mustn't for rules.","explanation_ar":"القواعد."},{"q":"Shouting at your friends is ___.","options":["allowed","respectful","polite","rude"],"answer":"rude","explanation":"Manners or safety word.","explanation_ar":"كلمة الآداب."},{"q":"","options":["My sister's helmet is pink.","My sisters's helmet is pink.","My sisters helmet is pink.","My sister helmet is pink."],"answer":"My sister's helmet is pink.","explanation":"Possessive apostrophe ('s / s').","explanation_ar":"الملكية."},{"q":"Should I bring a gift for the host? – Yes, you ___.","options":["should","shall","must to","do"],"answer":"should","explanation":"should / shouldn't for advice.","explanation_ar":"النصيحة."},{"q":"Pick the best tip for a new student:","options":["You should to ask questions when you don't understand.","You should asks questions when you don't understand.","You should ask questions when you don't understand.","You mustn't ask questions."],"answer":"You should ask questions when you don't understand.","explanation":"should / shouldn't for advice.","explanation_ar":"النصيحة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Yusuf and Omar welcoming a new boy at the school gate, handing him a booklet with a falcon logo, while a teacher waves from the principal's office. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Yusuf and Omar welcoming a new boy at the school gate, handing him a booklet with a falcon logo, while a teacher waves from the principal's office"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Rules and Manners”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Rules and Manners”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L04-U3-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin the Review Wheel”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin the Review Wheel"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS5-T1","script":"Welcome to our school! Here are some tips from Class 4A. You must greet the teachers when you enter the classroom, and you mustn't interrupt them. You don't have to bring lunch – the school's canteen has healthy food. You should wait in line at the canteen and say thank you. You shouldn't use other students' things without permission. Finally, you should visit the children's library. It's the best place in the school!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U3-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Guide to Good Manners: Language in Use”. Let’s learn must/mustn't/have to/don't have to, should, manners and safety words, possessive apostrophes (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Welcome team: one student is a new student from another country. The welcome team explains 3 rules (must/mustn't), 2 things he doesn't have to do and gives 2 pieces of advice (should). Today you use all of Unit 3: must/mustn't, have to/don't have to, should/shouldn't, manners and safety words, and possessive apostrophes. A guide gives clear rules (must) and friendly tips (should). It speaks to the reader as you. Here are some examples. You must wear the school's uniform. You mustn't run in the corridors. You don't have to buy books – the school gives them. Be careful! Some learners say: “You must to wear a uniform.” That’s not right. We say: “You must wear a uniform.” No to after must. Quick check: what is wrong with “You mustn't bring lunch – the canteen has food.”? … Think! … It should be “You don't have to bring lunch.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can explain rules and give advice to a new student.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"Everyone ___ wear a seat belt in the car.","options":["don't have to","must","mustn't","musts"],"answer":"must","explanation":"must / have to + base verb = necessary.","explanation_ar":"الضرورة."},{"q":"You ___ touch the hot oven!","options":["must","mustn't","don't have to","have"],"answer":"mustn't","explanation":"mustn't = not allowed.","explanation_ar":"mustn't تعني ممنوع."},{"q":"We ___ wear a uniform on the school trip. We can wear normal clothes.","options":["mustn't","has to","don't have to","must"],"answer":"don't have to","explanation":"don't have to = not necessary.","explanation_ar":"don't have to تعني غير ضروري."},{"q":"","options":["My dad has to travel for work.","My dad have to travel for work.","My dad must to travel for work.","My dad has travel for work."],"answer":"My dad has to travel for work.","explanation":"he / she / it → has to / doesn't have to.","explanation_ar":"المفرد الغائب ← has to."},{"q":"\"It isn't necessary to pay. The event is free.\" = You ___ pay.","options":["must","mustn't","don't have to","should to"],"answer":"don't have to","explanation":"don't have to = not necessary.","explanation_ar":"don't have to تعني غير ضروري."},{"q":"You have a headache. You ___ drink some water and rest.","options":["should to","shouldn't","should","mustn't"],"answer":"should","explanation":"should + base verb = advice (good idea).","explanation_ar":"should للنصيحة."},{"q":"You ___ play video games all night.","options":["shouldn't","must to","should","don't should"],"answer":"shouldn't","explanation":"shouldn't + base verb = a bad idea.","explanation_ar":"shouldn't للنهي اللطيف."},{"q":"","options":["Should I call my grandma tonight?","Do I should call my grandma tonight?","Should I to call my grandma tonight?","I should call my grandma tonight?"],"answer":"Should I call my grandma tonight?","explanation":"Should + subject + base verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ Should."},{"q":"","options":["He should eats more vegetables.","He should eat more vegetables.","He should to eat more vegetables.","He shoulds eat more vegetables."],"answer":"He should eat more vegetables.","explanation":"No to after must; must has no -s.","explanation_ar":"لا to بعد must."},{"q":"Which one is advice, not a rule?","options":["You must stop at the red light.","You mustn't park here.","Students must wear a uniform.","I think you should join the club."],"answer":"I think you should join the club.","explanation":"should = advice; must = rule.","explanation_ar":"الفرق بين should وmust."},{"q":"Interrupting the teacher is ___.","options":["safe","allowed","rude","polite"],"answer":"rude","explanation":"polite ↔ rude.","explanation_ar":"مهذب ↔ وقح."},{"q":"Always wear a ___ when you skate.","options":["seat belt","guest","uniform","helmet"],"answer":"helmet","explanation":"Choose the safety word that fits.","explanation_ar":"كلمة السلامة المناسبة."},{"q":"Please ___ turns on the swing.","options":["have","do","make","take"],"answer":"take","explanation":"Use the right manners or safety collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"You must ___ permission to leave early.","options":["ask for","take","make","give"],"answer":"ask for","explanation":"Use the right manners or safety collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"In American English, we ___ for the bus.","options":["wait in row","wait in line","stay in queue","queue at line"],"answer":"wait in line","explanation":"American English: wait in line.","explanation_ar":"الإنجليزية الأمريكية: wait in line."},{"q":"People who visit our home are our ___.","options":["guests","uniforms","rules","helmets"],"answer":"guests","explanation":"Use the right manners or safety collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"This is my ___ phone. (one brother)","options":["brothers","brothers'","brother","brother's"],"answer":"brother's","explanation":"One owner → 's.","explanation_ar":"المالك المفرد ← 's."},{"q":"The ___ changing room is on the right. (many players)","options":["player's","players's","players","players'"],"answer":"players'","explanation":"Plural owner ending in -s → s'.","explanation_ar":"المالك الجمع ← s'."},{"q":"","options":["The children' hospital is very modern.","The childrens hospital is very modern.","The children's hospital is very modern.","The childrens' hospital is very modern."],"answer":"The children's hospital is very modern.","explanation":"Irregular plural (children, men, women) → 's.","explanation_ar":"الجمع الشاذ ← 's."},{"q":"","options":["We bought three new chairs'.","We bought three new chair's.","We bought three new chairs's.","We bought three new chairs."],"answer":"We bought three new chairs.","explanation":"A simple plural has no apostrophe.","explanation_ar":"الجمع العادي بلا فاصلة علوية."},{"q":"","options":["Lina's scarf is blue.","Lina scarf is blue.","Linas' scarf is blue.","Linas scarf is blue."],"answer":"Lina's scarf is blue.","explanation":"One owner → 's.","explanation_ar":"المالك المفرد ← 's."},{"q":"Pick the best rule for a library sign:","options":["You mustn't to talk loudly in the library.","You mustn't talk loudly in the library.","You must not talks loudly in the library.","You don't have to talk loudly in the library."],"answer":"You mustn't talk loudly in the library.","explanation":"mustn't = not allowed.","explanation_ar":"mustn't تعني ممنوع."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"you must to ask for permision.\"","options":["You must ask for permision.","You must to ask for permission.","You must ask for permission.","you must ask for permission."],"answer":"You must ask for permission.","explanation":"No to after must; must has no -s.","explanation_ar":"لا to بعد must."},{"q":"Do we have to bring our own water? – ___","options":["No, you mustn't. The school has water.","No, you don't. The school has water.","No, you don't have. The school has water.","No, you aren't. The school has water."],"answer":"No, you don't. The school has water.","explanation":"don't have to = not necessary.","explanation_ar":"don't have to تعني غير ضروري."}],"theme_ar":"القواعد والآداب","essential_question_ar":"لماذا نحتاج إلى القواعد والأخلاق الحسنة؟","can_do":"I can explain rules with must, mustn't, have to and don't have to, give advice with should, and show possession with apostrophes.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أشرح القواعد باستخدام must وmustn't وhave to وdon't have to، وأقدّم النصيحة بـ should، وأعبّر عن الملكية بالفاصلة العلوية."});
